t of stock  in what roger goodell said to espn from  the standpoint of it opening some door  or breaking some barrier to me when i  hear the words when i see the delivery i  just think he answered the question the  only way he could  if he wants him back in the nfl  there's an easy way to make it happen  and we mentioned the president that that  is one of the things that may be keeping  a team from signing colin kaepernick  roger goodell also told mike greenberg  the nfl will continue to focus on our  work despite any criticism from the  president but i still feel like at some  level there is a hesitation  to engage the president in a full-blown  back and forth constant battle  on social media or elsewhere and i just  want to see the league get to the point  where they just don't care and the best  way to show you don't care is to get  colin kaepernick on a team  well yeah it is and and to support the  players for kneeling for the anthem if  that's what they decide to do as far as  their form of peaceful protest whatever  that may be but yeah the nfl needs to  support that um and i i mean again yeah  you know donald trump he's gonna  continue the president's gonna continue  to stick his nose into this situation we  know that you know he's he's obviously  passionate about it do i think he's  wrong about his feelings and and why  it's done of course i do i mean it's  really wrong but i do think the nfl's  best course of action at this point is  to just stay steadfast and go forward  with what we're doing right now we've  seen more progress and it feels like the  nfl and the important decision makers  have opened their eyes more here  recently than ever before and i think  you know as we've talked about there's  real momentum not only in our country  but in the nfl to get things changed  we've never seen it kind of move this  much in this short of a time and i just  think with this one yes it does the nfl  no good to get in a little fight or a  tit-for-tat fight with you know the  president none of that ignore it move on  we feel as the nfl we're doing the right  thing for society for our players and um  sorry mr president we disagree with you  and that's all there has to be said  about the situation  yeah i mean this fear that still seems  to be paralyzing the nfl when it comes  to taking on the president when it comes  to taking on the percentage of the fan  base that still insists that kneeling  during the national anthem automatically  constitutes disrespect of the flag the  military the the country no matter how  many different people come out and say  that's really not what it is they got to  get past that fear and whether it's  in making clear public statements  by owners not the commissioner that  there is support for protests during the  anthem by signing colin kaepernick by  changing the washington name these are  the things that would send the loudest  clearest message that the events of the  past 22 days the cumulative events from  the george floyd murder up to the rachar  brooks murder and all the protests and  the awakening and the piercing of our  bubble that this has caused and the  commitment to change and so many people  now involved in speaking out and finding  ways to assist  to show that the nfl truly gets it and  truly has had the same awakening the  rest of the country has had most of the  rest of the country has had those are  the things that need to happen  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

